{
  "issue" : 991,
  "description" : "Shared case table for the unified «Hoy» rule (issue #991 S2/S3/S6). Every platform's planning suite asserts its resolver against these cases. Day semantics: dates are local calendar days without time. `planned` and `due` are whole-day offsets relative to today in the device's local calendar (negative = past, 0 = today, positive = future; null = no date). `legacyScheduledForToday` models rows written by pre-#991 clients (the boolean that plannedDate replaces); `recurringInstance` is informational. Expected buckets are exclusive for active tasks (exactly one of today/upcoming/inbox is true); `postponed` (S6) is only meaningful when today is true: the planned day is strictly before today and is what places the task in «Hoy».",
  "cases" : [
    {
      "name" : "planned today, no due",
      "planned" : 0,
      "due" : null,
      "status" : "active",
      "expected" : {
        "today" : true,
        "postponed" : false,
        "upcoming" : false,
        "inbox" : false
      }
    },
    {
      "name" : "planned yesterday, no due (postponed — S6)",
      "planned" : -1,
      "due" : null,
      "status" : "active",
      "expected" : {
        "today" : true,
        "postponed" : true,
        "upcoming" : false,
        "inbox" : false
      }
    },
    {
      "name" : "planned long past, no due (still today, never rolls back to inbox)",
      "planned" : -30,
      "due" : null,
      "status" : "active",
      "expected" : {
        "today" : true,
        "postponed" : true,
        "upcoming" : false,
        "inbox" : false
      }
    },
    {
      "name" : "due yesterday, no plan (overdue — not postponed)",
      "planned" : null,
      "due" : -1,
      "status" : "active",
      "expected" : {
        "today" : true,
        "postponed" : false,
        "upcoming" : false,
        "inbox" : false
      }
    },
    {
      "name" : "planned yesterday and due today (stale plan reads as postponed)",
      "planned" : -1,
      "due" : 0,
      "status" : "active",
